<title>FINLAND: SBC WARBURG CUTS NOKIA TO REDUCE.</title>
<headline>SBC WARBURG CUTS NOKIA TO REDUCE.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Investment bank SBC Warburg has lowered its recommendtation on telecommunications group Nokia to reduce from hold due to the share's sharp gains, Warburg analyst Per Lindberg told Reuters on Thursday.</p>
<p>SBC Warburg's earnings forecasts for Nokia were intact -- at 6.89 billion markka pretax in 1997 and 8.49 billion in 1998 -- but &quot;the share has become too expensive&quot;, Lindberg said.</p>
<p>Warburg's price target is 360 markka, he said.</p>
<p>At 1200/0900 GMT, Nokia traded at 424.50 markka, down 5.80.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
